## Testing Layers in Isolation vs Full Stack

```
Test Level          | What's Real         | What's Mocked       | Speed
--------------------|---------------------|---------------------|--------
Unit                | Class under test    | All collaborators   | Fastest
@WebMvcTest         | HTTP + Controller   | Services, Repos     | Fast
@DataJpaTest        | JPA + Repository    | Services, Web       | Medium
@SpringBootTest     | Everything          | Nothing (ideally)   | Slowest

Test Distribution (ideal pyramid):
  70% Unit tests
  20% Controller + Service slice tests
  10% Full integration tests
```

## Production Reality

Keep integration tests to a minimum — 5-20 tests per application covering: happy path of critical flows (order creation, payment processing), authentication (403/401 for protected endpoints), cross-component interactions (event publishing → event handler → DB update). Use the test pyramid: many unit tests, few integration tests. Integration tests are valuable for catching wiring issues: "does the whole thing hang together?" not "does every edge case work?" — that's for unit tests.
